worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_16.js"
  ceiling 1281
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver: issue #658 divided one oversized worker file by line count, so this shard has no subject of its own. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Re-measured 2026-09-22 after the specification-red batch (bb43dbe90) mirrored the courtesy-frame guard into this shard (strip every courtesy and directive surface longest-first before an unknown fallback answers), growing the mirrored file from 1307 to 1336 lines; the ceiling records the measured size and should fall again when the twin moves behind js/wasm-worker. Ceiling 1335 (2026-10-08, issue #1165): the write_program answer hands the native report the page a documentation-sourced program was rediscovered from, so the server reports it as rediscovered rather than borrowing the language's recorded run. Lowered to 1278 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the research comparison table and result follow-up read data/seed/research-table-procedure.lino and seeded responses like the native handlers, and the memorized topic cells, the hardcoded column labels and the follow-up phrase list are gone. Ceiling moved 1278 to 1279: an unsupported write_program request yields to a seeded fact (issue #1175 p112, 2026-10-08), as the native unsupported request reaches meta dispatch where the fact_lookup row answers first. Ceiling moved 1279 to 1281 (2026-10-08, issue #1173 R1173-3): tryWriteProgram answers the print_text operand task with the program operandProgram composes and its bound run contract, as try_write_operand_program does natively."
